---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="China Visa Guide: Transit & Visa-Free Options"
  description="China visa options: 144-hour transit visa-free in 27 cities, 15-day visa-free for 30+ nationalities, tourist L visa process, costs, and requirements."
  canonicalUrl="/plan-trip/visa"
  articleDate="2026-08-03"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Plan Your Trip", url: "/plan-trip/" }, { name: "Visa Guide", url: "/plan-trip/visa/" }]}>
  <section class="pt-24 pb-16"><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#b5343a] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase">Plan Your Trip · Visa Guide</span>
    <h1 class="font-serif-sc text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-stone-900 mt-3">China Visa Guide: Which Option Is Right for You?</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">China''s entry policies have been rapidly relaxing. Depending on your nationality, you may not even need a visa for a focused traditional clothing trip.</p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5"><span class="text-xs px-2 py-0.5 bg-green-100 text-green-700 rounded-full font-medium">Easiest</span><h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mt-2">15-Day Visa-Free</h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">30+ countries including most of Western Europe, Australia, New Zealand, Malaysia. Just show up with your passport. No forms, no fees.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5"><span class="text-xs px-2 py-0.5 bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 rounded-full font-medium">Flexible</span><h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mt-2">144-Hour Transit</h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">27 cities. Arrive from Country A, depart to Country B. Stay up to 6 days in the approved region. No visa. Most nationalities qualify.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5"><span class="text-xs px-2 py-0.5 bg-stone-500 text-white rounded-full font-medium">Standard</span><h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mt-2">Tourist L Visa</h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">For longer stays or nationals not covered by visa-free. Apply at CVASC. 4-7 business days. 30-150 USD.</p></div>
    </div>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-16 mb-4">15-Day Visa-Free: The Easy Option</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Available to citizens of 30+ countries (list expanding regularly — check before travel). Requirements: valid passport (6+ months validity), return/onward flight ticket. No forms, no advance applications, no fees. Enter through any international port. Stay up to 15 days from midnight of arrival day.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-2 mt-4 mb-4">
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">France</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Germany</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Italy</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Spain</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Netherlands</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Switzerland</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Australia</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">New Zealand</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Malaysia</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Ireland</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Austria</span></div>
      <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-2.5 text-xs"><span class="font-medium text-green-800">Belgium</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-stone-400">Partial list as of 2026. Check with your nearest Chinese embassy for the latest eligible nationalities — China has been expanding this list every 6-12 months.</p>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">144-Hour Transit: Strategic Entry</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Key rule: arrive from Country A, depart to Country B. Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan count as separate destinations. A cheap flight or ferry to Hong Kong (as low as 50 USD) turns any round-trip into a valid transit itinerary.</p>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">L Visa: Step by Step</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Apply at your nearest CVASC. Required: passport, completed form, passport photo, flight + hotel bookings, itinerary. 4-7 business days. Visa agencies (VisaHQ, iVisa) handle the process for 50-100 USD extra.</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">How to Apply for an L Visa</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-stone-600">
      <p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Gather documents: passport (valid 6+ months beyond entry, 2+ blank pages), completed visa application form (Form V.2013), passport photo (33mm x 48mm, white background), flight itinerary, hotel bookings, and bank statements showing sufficient funds.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Submit at your nearest Chinese Visa Application Service Center (CVASC) or Chinese embassy/consulate. Most countries now require in-person fingerprinting. Processing time: 4-5 business days standard, 2-3 days express (extra fee).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Pay the fee. Single-entry L visa: ~140 USD (varies by nationality). Double-entry: ~210 USD. Multiple-entry (6-12 months): ~280-420 USD.</p>
      <p><strong>Tip:</strong> If visiting for traditional clothing experiences, list "cultural tourism" as your purpose. Include your Hanfu/qipao rental confirmations as supporting documents — this helps establish a legitimate travel itinerary.</p>
    </div>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">Embassy Links by Country</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">Find your nearest Chinese embassy or visa center: <a href="https://www.visaforchina.cn" class="text-[#b5343a] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">visaforchina.cn</a> (global portal). For US citizens: check your state's CVASC jurisdiction at the Chinese Embassy DC website. For EU citizens: most countries have CVASC centers in major cities.</p>
    
    <div class="mt-8"><a href="/plan-trip" class="text-sm text-stone-400 hover:text-stone-600 transition-colors">Back to Plan Your Trip</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
